HINT FULL: new pods are rejected (exceeded quota); find oversized requests first, then raise hard
HINT NEAR: under 15% headroom: a rollout surge can be rejected; plan the bump before the deploy
HINT OVERQUOTA: hard is 4x or more the use: shrink it and give the capacity back to the cluster
HINT OVERREQUEST: requests far above actual use: lower requests (VPA recommend, oc adm top) to free schedulable capacity
HINT UNDERREQUEST: pods use more than they request: raise requests or they are throttled or evicted first under node pressure
HINT NOMETRICS: no PodMetrics for this namespace: check metrics-server before trusting right-sizing
HINT INVALID: quota value is not a valid quantity (or hard is 0): fix the object, the check cannot reason about it
